{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.125.050","page_type":"section"},"citation":"5.125.050","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.125.050","content_hash":"e798d547f990e92a8002c6a9d352191408662ca86f42f2c7e0013dedb02eea08","heading":"Record of transactions.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.125.050:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.125.050","text":"(a) At the time of purchasing precious metal, a precious metal dealer shall enter in a book kept for that purpose:\n(1) The date of purchase;\n(2) A full and accurate description of each item purchased, including any identifying letters, numbers or marks on the item; and\n(3) The name, age, residence and driver’s license or other personal identification number of the seller.\n(b) The record required by this section shall be maintained by the precious metal dealer at the dealer’s place of business for not less than one year following the date of the transaction. (Code 1981 § 37-53. Code 1995 § 30-190.)\nState Law References: Record of transactions, K.S.A. 16-716 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"355a747c-40b8-5ed5-85b8-a689743bbee4"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.125.050","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.125.050","content_hash":"26b76b6b0fdb9888016f8a38b0714305ac1aefa2212273012ea4a4162779ab73","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.125.050:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.125.050:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.125.050","text":"(a) At the time of purchasing precious metal, a precious metal dealer shall enter i